WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:14.200
On November 26th, 2017 Honduras held elections,
some very peculiar elections:

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:17.640
Even though millions of people were called
on to vote that day, only one vote really

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:18.860
counted in the end:

00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:24.210
that of President Juan Orlando Hernández,
who decided to stay for another four years,

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:33.480
no matter what the polls said.

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:46.160
Yes, President Hernandez very probably just
told himself: “Hey, if I like being President

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:47.320
so much...

00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:49.260
why leave?!”

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:53.899
Since then protests, due to what has obviously
been a rigged election, an assault on democracy,

00:00:53.899 --> 00:00:55.829
have occurred quite frequently.

00:00:55.829 --> 00:00:59.810
Honduras is a country that already suffers
from the tragic consequences of a social and

00:00:59.810 --> 00:01:02.110
political model full of corruption and violence.

00:01:02.110 --> 00:01:06.890
A model, dear viewer, that is so disastrous
and dysfunctional that it led Honduras to

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:11.141
be the poorest country in Latin America, and
the third most dangerous country in the world

00:01:11.141 --> 00:01:18.090
(which is not at war).

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:24.670
See, Honduras is a small tropical country,
with just over 9 million inhabitants, located

00:01:24.670 --> 00:01:29.730
on a narrow strip of land that separates the
Caribbean Sea from the Pacific Ocean.

00:01:29.730 --> 00:01:35.549
Indeed, Honduras is one of those places where
we can find some of the most incredible beaches

00:01:35.549 --> 00:01:36.860
in the world...

00:01:36.860 --> 00:01:43.280
White sandy, crystal clear waters, and lots
of coconut trees.

00:01:43.280 --> 00:01:45.530
Sounds rather nice, doesn’t it?

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:50.330
Unfortunately though, drug trafficking, gangs
and a political and economic elite have prioritized,

00:01:50.330 --> 00:01:52.890
above all, plundering the nations resources.

00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:57.010
They have muddied and stained the reality
of a country that could otherwise be safe,

00:01:57.010 --> 00:02:13.560
and possibly even considered a true paradise
here on earth.

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:29.090
But hold on, you may be thinking... a small,
remote, poor country…

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:31.920
Just another drop in the ocean of problems,
right?

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:40.200
Well, wait a minutes because there’s a lot
more at work here...

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:44.790
What would you think if I told you we might
be facing the first coup d'état supported

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:46.370
by the Trump Administration?

00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:51.450
Well, check this out.

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:58.410
(THE FRAUD)

00:02:58.410 --> 00:03:03.470
On Sunday, November 26th, 2017, general elections
were held in Honduras.

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:08.100
There were two major contenders for the Presidency,
which is the most important political position

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:09.100
in the country:

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:13.570
On the one hand, President Juan Orlando Hernández,
who was widely supported by the country’s

00:03:13.570 --> 00:03:18.720
economic leadership and the international
community, aspired to be re-elected.

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:23.611
A reelection that, by the way, was very controversial,
because, in principle, the country’s Constitution

00:03:23.611 --> 00:03:28.900
prevents it under article 239; an article
that was declared inapplicable in 2015 by

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:32.490
a surprising and a very controversial decision
from the Supreme Court.

00:03:32.490 --> 00:03:37.240
But do bear in mind here, that the supreme
court in actuality is “controlled” by

00:03:37.240 --> 00:03:38.420
the President.

00:03:38.420 --> 00:03:50.180
So that might have had something to do with
it.

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:52.709
This is what article 239 said:

00:03:52.709 --> 00:03:58.849
( “If a citizen has held the ownership of
the Executive Power, he or she cannot be the

00:03:58.849 --> 00:03:59.849
president or designee.”

00:03:59.849 --> 00:04:02.870
Article 239 of the Honduran Constitution.)

00:04:02.870 --> 00:04:07.940
Now, on the other hand, Salvador Nasralla,
a popular television presenter, ran as candidate

00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:14.310
for the center-left parties’ coalition,
the Opposition Alliance.

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:36.340
Well, the fact is that in the initial vote
count, everything pointed to Salvador Nasralla’s

00:04:36.340 --> 00:04:37.529
victory.

00:04:37.529 --> 00:04:42.990
See, with almost 60% of the votes counted
for, he had a 5-point lead over the President...

00:04:42.990 --> 00:04:46.960
The advantage was so overwhelming that the
magistrates who form the Honduras Supreme

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:51.820
Electoral Tribunal qualified this lead as
irreversible and insurmountable.

00:04:51.820 --> 00:04:56.620
However, suddenly, counting stopped, there
was no additional information...

00:04:56.620 --> 00:05:01.099
computer systems collapsed, new ballots appeared
and in the end… several days later…

00:05:01.099 --> 00:05:14.899
the Electoral Tribunal awarded a surprising
victory to President Juan Orlando Hernandez

00:05:14.899 --> 00:05:19.020
There were so many irregularities that the
Organization of American States itself rejected

00:05:19.020 --> 00:05:25.789
the recount and called for new elections.

00:05:25.789 --> 00:05:36.560
But that’s not all.

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:40.919
One day before the elections, The Economist
published on its website that it had a recording

00:05:40.919 --> 00:05:55.360
that proved that the government was preparing
to distort the results of the election.

00:05:55.360 --> 00:05:57.629
Anyway, was there a rigged election?

00:05:57.629 --> 00:06:02.830
Well, that’s hard to say, but the chances
are really high.

00:06:02.830 --> 00:06:04.939
All this without mentioning the government’s
authoritarian behavior.

00:06:04.939 --> 00:06:10.939
Of course, once the possibility of an electoral
fraud was on the table, the opposition mobilized

00:06:10.939 --> 00:06:12.939
and organized protest rallies.

00:06:12.939 --> 00:06:16.999
They were peaceful at first, but the police
didn’t seem to care, they still used as

00:06:16.999 --> 00:06:20.729
much force as they wanted...

00:06:20.729 --> 00:06:27.559
For example, on the evening of Wednesday 29th,
state forces fired tear gas at a rally of

00:06:27.559 --> 00:06:30.439
about 1,000 people who were peacefully awaiting
the results.

00:06:30.439 --> 00:06:33.930
Indeed in this group was the opposition candidate
Salvador Nasralla.

00:06:33.930 --> 00:06:37.460
The police didn’t care that it was a peaceful
concentration or that there were children

00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:54.449
and elderly people present.

00:06:54.449 --> 00:07:03.621
The 
government even decreed a curfew, and since

00:07:03.621 --> 00:07:09.979
then, rallies have been put down with 30 people
being killed and more than 800 detainees.

00:07:09.979 --> 00:07:14.159
In other words, evidence points to a clearly
rigged election, followed by forceful repression…

00:07:14.159 --> 00:07:26.520
all to reinforce 

00:07:26.520 --> 00:07:27.620
the victory.

00:07:27.620 --> 00:07:31.309
Now, having said that, we have several questions
that need an answer.

00:07:31.309 --> 00:07:34.209
And clearly, one of them is, who exactly is
the President?

00:07:34.209 --> 00:07:37.009
Who is Juan Orlando Hernández?

00:07:37.009 --> 00:07:39.869
(THE PRESIDENT)

00:07:39.869 --> 00:07:49.629
There are two versions, two very different
interpretations of President Hernández.

00:07:49.629 --> 00:07:54.110
The first is that of a leader with a strong
hand but who can rescue his country from becoming

00:07:54.110 --> 00:07:55.110
a failed state.

00:07:55.110 --> 00:07:59.520
The second is that of an authoritarian leader,
involved in corruption and crime, a leader

00:07:59.520 --> 00:08:04.999
who has taken control of the country's institutions
and who manages them based on his own interests....

00:08:04.999 --> 00:08:08.649
As we saw in the case of the Supreme Court
and re-election….

00:08:08.649 --> 00:08:24.909
However, the President, and we will see this
in more detail in a moment, has the support

00:08:24.909 --> 00:08:27.129
of the United States, among others.

00:08:27.129 --> 00:08:32.729
And to be fair, we must say that his mandate
has had many dark times, but also some good

00:08:32.729 --> 00:08:33.729
ones.

00:08:33.729 --> 00:08:40.849
Let's start with these, the good times.

00:08:40.849 --> 00:08:47.149
See, when Juan Orlando Hernández came to
power in 2013, Honduras had the highest homicide

00:08:47.149 --> 00:08:59.149
rate of a country not at war.

00:08:59.149 --> 00:09:03.310
It is true that nowadays the country still
has a serious problem, it is still ranked

00:09:03.310 --> 00:09:08.459
third as the country with most homicides in
relation to its population - further, 90%

00:09:08.459 --> 00:09:11.490
of these crimes remain unpunished.

00:09:11.490 --> 00:09:12.950
But things have improved.

00:09:12.950 --> 00:09:16.990
In fact, this is the President’s main pride
and joy.

00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:21.660
With help from the United States, the government
of Honduras has created a new special police

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:26.220
force, financed, equipped and trained by the
DEA and the FBI, among others.

00:09:26.220 --> 00:09:30.570
At the same time, it has expelled and replaced
thousands of corrupt agents; it has dismantled

00:09:30.570 --> 00:09:35.540
several drug cartels and extradited dozens
of drug traffickers to the United States.

00:09:35.540 --> 00:09:39.240
It even created parks throughout the country,
which are guarded by the military police,

00:09:39.240 --> 00:09:46.310
so that children and families can enjoy their
leisure time safely.

00:09:46.310 --> 00:09:55.280
So far so good, right?

00:09:55.280 --> 00:10:00.820
Unfortunately, dear viewer, the story doesn’t
end there with rainbows and butterflies...

00:10:00.820 --> 00:10:08.660
There is clear evidence of the President's
corruption.

00:10:08.660 --> 00:10:13.529
In fact, the 2013 election campaign that brought
him to power was financed by money stolen

00:10:13.529 --> 00:10:16.300
from the Honduran Institute of Social Security.

00:10:16.300 --> 00:10:20.310
And there are even well-founded suspicions
that President Orlando has had connections

00:10:20.310 --> 00:10:22.100
with drug-trafficking groups.

00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:27.870
( “The illegal drug trade in Honduras not
only infected much of its civil society, including

00:10:27.870 --> 00:10:32.160
the highest levels of government and its financial
sector, but also brought frightening levels

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:37.540
of violence on its people,” Joon H. Kim,
the acting UnVited States attorney in Manhattan.)

00:10:37.540 --> 00:10:42.190
In any case, whether these accusations are
true or not, repression, deception and controlling

00:10:42.190 --> 00:10:47.089
institutions can neither be justified nor
contribute to Honduras being able to overcome

00:10:47.089 --> 00:10:49.510
the problems that impede its development.

00:10:49.510 --> 00:10:55.110
The president has clear support from the international
community, he has received money, police aid,

00:10:55.110 --> 00:10:56.930
military and political support.

00:10:56.930 --> 00:11:00.300
And, the truth is, the people expected something
different.

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:06.920
Of course, dear viewer, all this isn’t strange
in this country.

00:11:06.920 --> 00:11:14.019
(A COCKTAIL OF CORRUPTION AND VIOLENCE)

00:11:14.019 --> 00:11:15.600
Honduras is facing a difficult problem…

00:11:15.600 --> 00:11:20.790
There is a triangle of interrelated powers
that make being an optimist in Honduras very

00:11:20.790 --> 00:11:26.290
difficult: political power, the economic oligarchy
and drug traffickers.

00:11:26.290 --> 00:11:33.060
Perhaps the most representative case of all
is that of Fabio Lobo, the son of Porfirio

00:11:33.060 --> 00:11:37.490
Lobo, the former President of the Republic,
who has just been sentenced in the United

00:11:37.490 --> 00:11:42.899
States to 24 years in prison for his involvement
and activities as a drug trafficker.

00:11:42.899 --> 00:11:45.319
He actually did this when his father was President
of the Republic.

00:11:45.319 --> 00:11:48.820
And no, we’re not talking about a rebellious
son or anything like that…

00:11:48.820 --> 00:12:02.580
Drug trafficking, by the way, is currently
the country's main economic activity.

00:12:02.580 --> 00:12:05.209
Another example, as the New York Times reported,
is parliament:

00:12:05.209 --> 00:12:10.360
It’s an under-equipped building from the
50s, that lacks the minimum necessary conditions,

00:12:10.360 --> 00:12:14.279
which contrast with the deputies’ parking
lot, a parking lot that is full of off-road

00:12:14.279 --> 00:12:17.370
vehicles, all the latest and most expensive
models.

00:12:17.370 --> 00:12:25.050
And this affects practically everyone, the
government and opposition.

00:12:25.050 --> 00:12:27.720
The police and security forces aren’t removed
from this either.

00:12:27.720 --> 00:12:31.480
Extortion and bribery is common, and it is
widely known that police members have ties

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:33.779
with gangs and drug-traffickers.

00:12:33.779 --> 00:12:39.259
( “Mara Salvatrucha gangsters in Rivera
Hernández say they receive warnings from

00:12:39.259 --> 00:12:43.910
the police of impending sweeps and are handed
captured rivals to execute, for anything from

00:12:43.910 --> 00:12:48.040
$440 to $2,200 a head.

00:12:48.040 --> 00:12:50.960
- Sonia Nazario, Pulitzer Prize winning journalist)

00:12:50.960 --> 00:13:01.160
Politicians, security forces, gangs, drug-traffickers...
and lastly the economic oligarchy.

00:13:01.160 --> 00:13:06.209
Ten families control practically every economic
resource and have had no problems paying bribes

00:13:06.209 --> 00:13:10.480
and placing trustworthy people in the powerful
positions to generate something that is not

00:13:10.480 --> 00:13:14.970
a market model, but a model that is entirely
controlled by the institutions.

00:13:14.970 --> 00:13:19.470
Well, all of this dear viewer, makes up a
highly extractive resource network, and is

00:13:19.470 --> 00:13:23.810
ultimately responsible for Honduras not being
that paradise we discussed at the beginning

00:13:23.810 --> 00:13:24.810
of the video.

00:13:24.810 --> 00:13:28.930
But we also mentioned the US government, specifically
the Trump Administration, as possibly being

00:13:28.930 --> 00:13:33.730
responsible for what happened with Honduras’
elections.

00:13:33.730 --> 00:13:40.430
So, let’s get to it...

00:13:40.430 --> 00:13:43.110
(WASHINGTON’S IMPORTANCE)

00:13:43.110 --> 00:13:48.580
You could be forgiven for initially thinking
that Honduras is not that important to Washington,

00:13:48.580 --> 00:13:49.580
right?

00:13:49.580 --> 00:13:50.580
Well... not exactly.

00:13:50.580 --> 00:13:56.499
The truth is that Honduras has a certain importance
in the United States, for three main reasons:

00:13:56.499 --> 00:14:02.279
first because a lot of the flights suspected
of transporting drugs from South America have

00:14:02.279 --> 00:14:04.290
their first stop in this country.

00:14:04.290 --> 00:14:08.819
Secondly, because two years ago, faced with
the country’s enormous crisis, 18,000 Honduran

00:14:08.819 --> 00:14:11.399
children travelled alone to the United States
border.

00:14:11.399 --> 00:14:15.290
And nobody in Washington wants that to happen
again.

00:14:15.290 --> 00:14:19.880
Thirdly, because Honduras has traditionally
been an allied country, in fact, the United

00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:21.860
States has had a military base there for decades.

00:14:21.860 --> 00:14:26.060
Due to all this, the US has spent billions
of dollars in Honduras in recent years, to

00:14:26.060 --> 00:14:28.339
try to reverse the country's problems.

00:14:28.339 --> 00:14:33.040
Well, the Trump Administration knows this,
and supports Juan Orlando Hernández.

00:14:33.040 --> 00:14:36.589
Indeed this is what a prominent Republican
adviser said about the matter:

00:14:36.589 --> 00:14:41.560
(“Washington has invested significant money
in Central America to help turn the security

00:14:41.560 --> 00:14:43.199
and economic situation around.

00:14:43.199 --> 00:14:47.059
if Hernández loses the election, the United
States will have no effective partners in

00:14:47.059 --> 00:14:50.610
the region, the effectiveness of our billions
of dollars would be at risk, and more people

00:14:50.610 --> 00:14:53.290
might be tempted to come to the United States.”

00:14:53.290 --> 00:14:57.949
Daniel Runde, a Republican foreign policy
adviser and former official in the George

00:14:57.949 --> 00:14:59.499
W. Bush administration)

00:14:59.499 --> 00:15:01.980
Yes, Washington's support is clear.

00:15:01.980 --> 00:15:06.120
In fact, the police, which were trained and
financed by the United States, participated

00:15:06.120 --> 00:15:13.319
in the post-electoral events, without any
complaint from the US embassy...

00:15:13.319 --> 00:15:17.550
And this is because the US government fears
the ties that Salvador Nasralla’scandidacy

00:15:17.550 --> 00:15:22.459
could have with the Cuban regime or even with
Nicolás Maduro’s Venezuela, something that

00:15:22.459 --> 00:15:23.899
incidentally, the candidate denies.

00:15:23.899 --> 00:15:28.801
(“They are wrong because my model is based
in Uruguay or Chile’s moderate left, or

00:15:28.801 --> 00:15:30.640
Costa Rica’s moderate right.

00:15:30.640 --> 00:15:35.569
One thing is the friendship that my ideological
partner, Manuel Zelaya, has with Maduro or

00:15:35.569 --> 00:15:40.550
Morales and something very different is what
I think, me who would be the president.”

00:15:40.550 --> 00:15:41.550
Salvador Nasralla.)

00:15:41.550 --> 00:15:47.139
Anyway, for everyone watching from Honduras,
we should state that things can change and

00:15:47.139 --> 00:15:48.149
do tend to change.

00:15:48.149 --> 00:15:50.060
There’s the case of Colombia, for example.

00:15:50.060 --> 00:15:51.430
And now it’s your turn.

00:15:51.430 --> 00:15:55.029
Do you think we’re facing the first coup
d'état backed by the Trump Administration?

00:15:55.029 --> 00:15:57.990
Well, leave your answer in the comments as
well as in the survey.

